1 SEX M
1 NOTE Elder twin son of Rama and Sita, born at Valmiki’s hermitage (Uttara Kanda). Ruled southern Kosala from Kushasthali/Kushavati.  Sources: Wikipedia, “Kusha (Ramayana)” (Uttara Kanda; Raghuvamsha: wife Kumudvati, son Atithi).
0 @lava@ INDI
1 NAME Lava //
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Younger twin son of Rama and Sita (Uttara Kanda). Ruled northern Kosala from Shravasti; traditionally linked with founding Lavapuri (Lahore).  Sources: Wikipedia, “Lava (Ramayana)” (Shravasti; Ananda Ramayana: wife Sumati).
0 @kumudvati@ INDI
1 NAME Kumudvati //
1 SEX F
1 NOTE Wife of Kusha, daughter of the Naga chief Kumuda (Raghuvamsha, canto 16). The Ananda Ramayana calls her Champika.  Sources: Wikipedia, “Kusha (Ramayana)” (Uttara Kanda; Raghuvamsha: wife Kumudvati, son Atithi).
0 @sumati_l@ INDI
1 NAME Sumati //
1 SEX F
1 NOTE Wife of Lava according to the Ananda Ramayana.  Sources: Wikipedia, “Lava (Ramayana)” (Shravasti; Ananda Ramayana: wife Sumati).
0 @atithi@ INDI
1 NAME Atithi //
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Son of Kusha and his heir (Raghuvamsha, canto 17).  Sources: Wikipedia, “Kusha (Ramayana)” (Uttara Kanda; Raghuvamsha: wife Kumudvati, son Atithi); Kalidasa, Raghuvamsha (via Wikipedia “Raghuvamsha”): Dilipa → Raghu → Aja (m. Indumati) → Dasharatha.
0 @angada_l@ INDI
1 NAME Angada (son of Lakshmana) //
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Son of Lakshmana and Urmila; given the kingdom of Karupada (Uttara Kanda). Not the same person as the vanara Angada, son of Vali.  Sources: Wikipedia, “Lakshmana” (Uttara Kanda: sons Angada & Chandraketu).
0 @chandraketu@ INDI
1 NAME Chandraketu //
1 SEX M
1 NOTE Son of Lakshmana and Urmila; ruled Malla with its capital Chandrakanti (Uttara Kanda).  Sources: Wikipedia, “Lakshmana” (Uttara Kanda: sons Angada & Chandraketu).
0 @taksha@ INDI
